## 7. Pager Dealing Loop ✅ STAGE 6 COMPLETE (now gated on §7.5)

The **schedule-disrupting engine** of the game. Not just income — the system that creates moment-to-moment dramatic choices.

**Reframe in v0.9:** This was previously the player's first dealing mechanic. It's now Stage 2 of the dealing track. The player must first do street dealing (§7.5) to pay back Hank and earn enough to buy a pager from Felix. Activating the pager is the moment the world "starts taking notice" of the player as a regular dealer — repeat customers seed, pages begin to fire, the HUD pager indicator appears.

### Pager as equipment

The pager is a purchasable item (Felix's pawn shop). Acquired via the existing player tool-dispatch path (`try_tool` / active item handler — same pattern that handles the watering can on plants and skateboard activation): with the pager in the active slot, press interact in open space to activate. The item is consumed; PagerSystem's `has_pager` flag is set; HUD indicator appears; starter customer seeds. One-way unlock — there's no losing the pager.

Before activation:
- HUD pager indicator is hidden
- `PagerSystem` does not generate pages (early-return on minute tick)
- CustomerRoster is empty
- The Appointment Panel is unreachable (no clickable icon)
- The Callback Panel at the payphone will open and show "No messages" — payphones have other future uses so the panel itself is not gated

After activation:
- All of the above wire up
- One-time notification ("Pager activated.")
- Starter customer (currently "Dee P.") seeds via the `pager_acquired` signal
- The pager loop is live

### The loop

1. **Page arrives** — pure interruption, you don't control timing. Pager indicator blinks on HUD
2. **Click pager or find payphone** — clicking pager shows appointments; payphone returns calls
3. **Return the call** — short scheduling — meet location auto-assigned, time auto-set 12+ hours out (with 0-6 hour jitter, rounded to 15-min increments), avoids sleep window
4. **Commit to a window** — buyer waits 60 in-game minutes at the spot
5. **Travel and execute** — get there during the window, talk → auto-sell if you have enough product, payout at retail (1.5× base value)
6. **Back to whatever you were doing**

### Implemented systems

- **Customer roster** — persistent list of customers across save sessions. Empty until pager acquired. Starter customer seeds on `pager_acquired`. New customers added in waves when player crosses DEX tier thresholds. Customers have tier (gate), affinity, trust, times_dealt, times_flaked, blacklisted flags.
- **PagerSystem** — drives time-driven page generation. Gated on `has_pager`. Each waking minute, each active customer rolls a small per-customer chance scaled by their tier. Per-customer cooldown (24h) prevents double-paging. Pages have 6-hour waking-time callback deadlines.
- **MeetingManager** — when player returns a call, schedules a meeting at an available `MeetSpot` at an available time. Spots register on `_ready`, persist in the manager. Window collision detection prevents simultaneous overlap at same spot.
- **MeetingSpawner** — listens to `meeting_started`, instantiates `CustomerNPC` at the spot during the active window. Despawns on completion/miss/window-close. Handles cross-room materialization on room change.
- **CustomerNPC** — interactable. Talk → if inventory has enough raw_bud, deduct + payout + complete; if not, prompt to come back with more.
- **AppointmentPanel** — clicking the pager icon opens a list of upcoming and active meetings. `[NOW]` prefix on active ones. Defensive gate: refuses to open pre-pager.

### Pager rep / DealerExperience

Per design doc, pager rep is the spine of progression for the dealing track. Implemented as `DealerExperience` autoload — single int XP, tier function, tier_unlocked signal. Awarded on completed sales (proportional to quantity sold). Penalized on missed callbacks and missed deals.

- **Tier thresholds:** [0, 25, 75, 150, 300] — tunable
- **XP per unit sold:** 1 (pager-mediated) or 1 (street, see §7.5)
- **Missed callback penalty:** -2
- **Missed deal penalty:** -5
- **Tier-up:** spawns wave of new customers into roster (per `WAVE_SIZE_PER_TIER`)

### Buyer relationship system

Each customer carries minimal versions of the NPC relationship axes:
- **Affinity** — friendliness toward player
- **Trust** — willingness to introduce friends, work bigger deals
- **times_dealt** / **times_flaked** — tracked for blacklisting

Repeat flakers (3+ no-show meetings or missed callbacks) get blacklisted automatically.

### Buyer archetypes (future content, post-MVP)

Customers are currently randomly generated from name/sprite pools. Eventually some customers become *named characters* with full dialogue trees — the recurring weekly Friday-afternoon college kid, the chatty late-night woman, the haggler. The data model already supports this; it's a content-authoring task.

