## §X Calling Cards

Replaces direct cash payment at payphone. Aligns with period-setting and creates ongoing errand cadence at bodega.

### Mechanic
- Calls cost a variable number of "minutes."
- Minutes live on physical calling card items in player inventory.
- Each calling card is an `ItemStack` with `data: {"minutes": N}` per-instance.
- Cards do not merge across denominations or remaining-minutes values.
- Inventory friction is intentional — each card is its own slot.

### Cost taxonomy (initial values, tunable)
- Pager callback (set up a deal): 1 minute
- NPC hangout / relationship call: variable, ~5-10 minutes
- Special calls (future content): TBD per call site

### SKUs (sold at bodega)
- 30-minute card: $5
- 120-minute card: $15

### Player start
- Single 30-min card item spawned with `minutes: 20` at game start.

