## 24. Player Skills ✅ STAGE 8 COMPLETE

The capability-progression spine that complements the content-gating XP tracks (DEX, CRIM).

### The distinction

- **XP tracks (DEX, CRIM)** gate content. New customers, tools, contacts. Player feels progression through "I can now do X."
- **Player skills** gate capability and access. Make moment-to-moment play feel better and slowly open up the world. Player feels progression through "I feel faster / I can carry more / I can reach places I couldn't before."

### Visibility model

- **No involuntary numbers.** No Skyrim "+1 Lockpicking" popups.
- **One-time threshold notifications.** "You feel quicker on your feet" — once.
- **Optional dedicated screen** (deferred). Stardew-style.

### Initial skill set

**Athletics (implemented)**
- XP accrues per pixel moved. Speed scales `1.0 + level * 0.015`. L50 = 140 px/s.
- Capability thresholds: `vault_low` at L10, `vault_medium` at L25, `vault_high` at L50.

**Vault (loosely implemented)**
- 1-tile-thick rule in traversal axis. Vaultable tiles in per-room `TileMap` named "Vaultables" with `vault_tier` custom data layer (0/1/2).
- Per-tier tuning shipped: duration 0.6s/0.8s/1.3s, arc 15/18/32px, XP 5/10/20.
- Single tween with parallel children for position + arc; chained callback for completion.
- Stamina cost: 2 per vault.

**Strength (loosely implemented)**
- XP accrues on movement × filled inventory slots.
- Inventory expands at L10/L20/L30/L40/L50: +6 slots each.

**Lockpicking (loosely implemented)**
- 3 XP per successful locked car loot.
- Duration scaling: `max(0.1, 1.0 - level * 0.012)`.

**Stealth (deferred until heat shipped — wait, heat is shipped; stealth is now the only deferred sub-piece of the heat surface, included in the deferred list §16)**
- Trigger: XP per second in witness viewport without being detected; larger XP on completed undetected crime.
- Effect: extends witness's "noticed" meter fill time.

**Street Read (post-MVP, design only)**
- Forthcoming skill, tied to street dealing. XP per deal initiated. Capability: passerby archetypes display visual tells more prominently.

### Movement tools (skateboard)

Athletics-track upgrade items that replace foot-speed with a flat speed from the item. Uses the existing tool framework (§17). Skateboard's `tool_id = &"skateboard"`, `movement_speed = 150.0`. Held active + interact in allowed scenes (outdoor neighborhoods) → enter skate mode. Drains stamina at 40% of walking rate. Auto-dismounts on room change to disallowed scenes. Persists across saves.

Pattern extends to future bike, rollerblades, etc.

### Vault

Vaultable objects throughout outdoor scenes — low fences, mid-height walls, dumpsters, rooftop ledges. Tier-gated. Becomes traversal progression — the world feels more open as Athletics levels.

### Cop pursuit vault interaction

Cops can't vault medium until high pursuit aggression. Documented as design intent; implementation slot in the pursuit state machine.

### Skill gates as content authoring lever

The biggest payoff of skills: they become a content-gating axis for events and quests:
- NPCs open up to high-stealth players (assumed-able-to-keep-secret)
- Specific Hank offers require lockpicking tier
- Rooftop-delivery questlines open at Athletics tier 3 (high vault unlock)
- Neighbor mentions the basement burglary if forced-entry skill is high enough

Players who skill into different things see different games.

### Architecture

- `PlayerSkills` autoload owns all skills via a single `SKILL_CONFIG` dict.
- Adding a new skill = new config entry + trigger wiring in the source system.
- One save dict, signals (`skill_changed`, `level_up`, `capability_unlocked`).
- Skills distinct from XP tracks: skills gate capability, XP tracks gate content.

### Open design questions

- Skill caps: tentatively each skill caps at ~50 levels.
- Whether to surface skills before first level-up or wait for threshold.

